=====================================

## ABOUT
========
emu16K is the reference emulator for the rezoid rzd16K
processor, written in C++03. it attempts to be
cycle-accurate and in the style of the MOS 6502 emulator
"fake6502", of which was written by Mike Chambers.

## COMPILING
============
to compile, run:
$ make -f mkf
to compile and run the created executable, run:
$ make -f mkf run
to remove the executable, run:
$ make -f mkf clr

